Ours.  Declarations gcc 14 needs in xdm:
each file that called a function with no declaration gets a prototype after its
includes, taken from the definition the call links with (gcc -aux-info).  A K&R
definition's narrow parameters are default-promoted in the prototype, as a K&R caller
passes them (char/short/their typedefs -> int, float -> double):
  programs/xdm/choose.c: ForEachChooserHost(CARD16 connectionType -> int)
  programs/xdm/policy.c: ValidAuthorization(short unsigned int name_length -> int); AcceptableDisplayAddress(CARD16 connectionType -> int)
  programs/xdm/xdmcp.c: RememberIndirectClient(CARD16 connectionType -> int); ForgetIndirectClient(CARD16 connectionType -> int); ForEachMatchingIndirectHost(CARD16 connectionType -> int); SetProtoDisplayAuthorization(short unsigned int authorizationNameLen -> int); IsIndirectClient(CARD16 connectionType -> int); UseChooser(CARD16 connectionType -> int)
Declared without a prototype (types not defined at that point, or called with varying
arguments; none has an ANSI definition with a narrow parameter): 
AcceptableDisplayAddress CheckAuthentication ForEachChooserHost 
ForEachMatchingIndirectHost ForgetIndirectClient IsIndirectClient 
RememberIndirectClient SelectAuthorizationTypeIndex send_accept send_decline 
send_unwilling send_willing UseChooser XdmcpAllocARRAY8 XdmcpReallocARRAY8 
XdmcpReallocARRAYofARRAY8 

